    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-129564",
      "knowledge_point_id": "d237f9fb-b5d2-53e0-bc28-ee50d9e08852",
      "knowledge_point": "Evaluating a Double Integral Over a Rectangular Domain",
      "problem": "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+4}\\,\\text{d}A,$ where \n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 3}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:      \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+4}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+4}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+4}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{y}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+4}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{y}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})]}_{0}^{2}\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{y}^{2}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡0)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{8}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\pi }{8}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\frac{\\pi }{8}(\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}){|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{24}({3}^{3}-{0}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi }{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
