      "math_academy_id": "q-129568",
      "knowledge_point_id": "d237f9fb-b5d2-53e0-bc28-ee50d9e08852",
      "knowledge_point": "Evaluating a Double Integral Over a Rectangular Domain",
      "problem": "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A,$ where \n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4},\\,0\\le y\\le \\pi \\}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:   \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }[{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\nMaking a substitution $x+y=u,$ $\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u,$ we get.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }[{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }[{\\int }_{y}^{y+\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }[\\operatorname{sin}⁡u]_{y}^{y+\\pi /4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y+\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y]\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y+\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y]\\text{d}y & ={[\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(y+\\frac{\\pi }{4})]}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{4}))-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡0-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})) \\\\  & =(-1+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})-(1-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
