      "math_academy_id": "q-72267",
      "knowledge_point_id": "d237f9fb-b5d2-53e0-bc28-ee50d9e08852",
      "knowledge_point": "Evaluating a Double Integral Over a Rectangular Domain",
      "problem": "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A,$ where \n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:   \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[{e}^{x+y}]}_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}({e}^{1+y}-{e}^{0+y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}({e}^{1+y}-{e}^{y})\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(e{e}^{y}-{e}^{y})\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{y}(e-1)\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{y}(e-1)\\text{d}y & =(e-1)[{e}^{y}]_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(e-1)({e}^{2}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =(e-1)({e}^{2}-1) \\\\  & ={e}^{3}-{e}^{2}-e+1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
