      "knowledge_point_id": "d8f012d0-444a-5035-8a72-a053de312d63",
      "knowledge_point": "Changing the Order of Integration",
      "problem": "Evaluate the repeated integral ${\\int }_{1}^{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{5}^{y}}{x}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{5}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{5}^{y}}{x}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}\\frac{1}{x}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}{5}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}\\frac{1}{x}{[\\frac{{5}^{y}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}]}_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}\\frac{1}{x}(\\frac{{5}^{1}-{5}^{0}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}\\frac{1}{x}(\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{5}\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡x]_{1}^{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1) \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$",
